# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Scriwo AI keys. ONE file for every AI platform.
#
#  1. Copy this file to  ai-keys.env  and paste your keys after the = signs.
#     Leave a line empty (or delete it) for a platform you do not use.
#  2. Put it on the server and apply it:
#       scp ai-keys.env scripts/apply-ai-keys.sh YOU@SERVER:/opt/wppflow-backend/
#       ssh YOU@SERVER
#       cd /opt/wppflow-backend && bash apply-ai-keys.sh
#     (or create ai-keys.env on the server with nano and run the last two lines)
#  3. The script adds the keys to .env, restarts the backend, then DELETES ai-keys.env.
#
#  Never commit this file or paste a key in chat. No spaces, no quotes around values.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Hosted platforms (free tiers exist for the first six) ────────────────────────────────────
GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Your own GPUs, or any OpenAI-compatible server (tried first when set) ────────────────────
AI_SELF_BASE_URL=
AI_SELF_MODEL=
AI_SELF_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: the order to try them in, for example  groq,gemini,openrouter ──────────────────
# Leave empty for the default: your own servers, Groq, Gemini, Cerebras, Mistral, NVIDIA, OpenRouter, Claude.
AI_PROVIDERS=

# ── Optional: keep customers' messages private ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1 = every company is limited to platforms that say they do not train on messages (Groq, Claude, your own servers)
AI_REQUIRE_NO_TRAINING=

# ── Optional: tell the app what a platform does with your data (no-training, may-train, unknown) ──
# Set AI_GEMINI_DATA=no-training only if your Google account is a paid one.
AI_GEMINI_DATA=
